<article class="env-lemma" id="0CW2">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/0CW2">Lemma <span data-tag="0CW2">77.6.2</span>.</a> Let $Y$ be an algebraic space over a scheme $S$. Let $g : X' \to X$ be a morphism of algebraic spaces over $Y$ with $X$ locally of finite type over $Y$. Let $\mathcal{F}$ be a quasi-coherent $\mathcal{O}_ X$-module. If $\text{Ass}_{X/Y}(\mathcal{F}) \subset g(|X'|)$, then for any morphism $Z \to Y$ we have $\text{Ass}_{X_ Z/Z}(\mathcal{F}_ Z) \subset g_ Z(|X'_ Z|)$. </p>
</article><article class="env-proof">
    <p>
      <strong>Proof.</strong>
      By Properties of Spaces, Lemma <a href="/tag/03H4" data-tag="03H4">66.4.3</a> the map $|X'_ Z| \to |X_ Z| \times _{|X|} |X'|$ is surjective as $X'_ Z$ is equal to $X_ Z \times _ X X'$. By Divisors on Spaces, Lemma <a href="/tag/0CV2" data-tag="0CV2">71.4.7</a> the map $|X_ Z| \to |X|$ sends $\text{Ass}_{X_ Z/Z}(\mathcal{F}_ Z)$ into $\text{Ass}_{X/Y}(\mathcal{F})$. The lemma follows. 
      <span class="qed">$\square$</span>
    </p>
</article>